    "# Weekly engineering report \u2014 October 29, 2026\n\nGood morning! Here is everything that happened this week, including the numbers you asked for. Grab a coffee; this one is long.\n\n## Release status\n\nWe shipped **syna-agent 2.5.1** on Tuesday. The release cost $3.50 per deployment to roll out (down from $5.00 in September), and it fixed 17 bugs, including the crash in `syna.server:main` that Dr. Chen reported on Jan. 5 while debugging the pod at 9 a.m. See https://github.com/Julynx/syna/releases for the full changelog, or visit www.syna-agent.dev/docs for the migration guide. The upgrade takes about 40 minutes.\n\n1. Update the pin: `uv tool install syna-agent`\n2. Run the migration: `syna migrate --dry-run`\n3. Verify the pod: `syna doctor`\n\n> Note: the old CLI flags still work, but they print a deprecation warning. We will remove them in 2.6.0, per the schedule discussed with Mrs. Robinson on Oct. 12.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe p99 latency dropped from 812 ms to 643 ms. Prof. Ramsey's team measured the improvement with the formula $$T_{p99} = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} t_i}{n} + \\epsilon$$ where \\(t_i\\) is the latency of request $i$ and $\\epsilon$ models scheduling noise. The scheduler gained a second queue for background jobs; the results were... surprising, to say the least.\n\n| Component | Before | After |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Router    | 210 ms | 140 ms|\n| Renderer  | 512 ms | 419 ms|\n\nThe ratio of goodput to overhead now stays above 3.5:1 even at 200 requests per second, which is the threshold we agreed on in the $12,000 budget memo. St. Louis and Madrid both hit 99.98% uptime. Wait... there is one caveat: the numbers exclude warm-up traffic, i.e. the first 60 seconds after each deploy.\n\n## Incident review\n\nOn Thursday the transcript pipeline wedged for 11 minutes. The root cause was a leaked file descriptor in the audio cache; Mr. Tanaka Jr. hot-patched it before the 23:59 backup window. The postmortem estimates the blast radius at 0.4% of sessions. Prof. Ramsey asked whether the same bug could affect the vision pipeline \u2014 the answer is no, and the reasoning is in appendix C of the report at www.syna-agent.dev/postmortems/2026-10-27.\n\nThe next review is on Monday at 9 a.m. sharp. Etc. \u2014 send comments before Friday. \ud83d\ude42\n",
